## Dependency Flow (Clean MVC Architecture)

```
index.js (boot)
  └── app.js (assemble Express)
        ├── middleware/ (auth, headers, rateLimit)
        └── routes/    (URL mapping only — no logic)
              └── controllers/ (request/response handling)
                    └── services/, lib/, db/ (pure business logic & data)
```

**Strict one-way dependency rule:**
- `routes/` → only import from `controllers/` and `middleware/`
- `controllers/` → only import from `services/`, `lib/`, and `db/`
- `services/` → never import from `routes/` or `controllers/`

This means any controller can be unit-tested by calling it directly without spinning up Express.

