### Layer 4: Route Modules

Each route file is intentionally **thin** — it only wires URL patterns to controller functions. Zero business logic lives here.

**Example pattern (how every route file will look):**
```js
// routes/agents.js
import { Router } from 'express';
import { auth, requireRole } from '../middleware/auth.js';
import * as agents from '../controllers/agents.controller.js';

const router = Router();
router.get('/',         auth, agents.list);
router.get('/:id',      auth, agents.getById);
router.get('/:id/anatomy', auth, agents.anatomy);
export default router;
```

